/**
 * @mainpage StripeKit C++
 *
 * StripeKit is a C++20 toolkit for integrating Stripe subscription billing
 * into an application: creating customers and Checkout sessions, offering a
 * self-serve billing portal, and reacting to the webhooks Stripe sends
 * afterwards.
 *
 * It keeps the Stripe work separate from the web framework underneath, so the
 * same billing code runs whichever framework the host application uses.
 *
 * @section main_start Getting started
 *
 * - @ref overview — what StripeKit does and how the pieces fit together.
 * - @ref quickstart — a working integration, step by step.
 *
 * @section main_reference Reference
 *
 * - @ref application_api — the API applications use to talk to Stripe.
 *   - @ref client — customers, Checkout, subscriptions, billing portal.
 *   - @ref models — the Stripe objects StripeKit returns.
 *   - @ref webhooks — verifying deliveries and handling each event once.
 *   - @ref errors — the exceptions StripeKit throws.
 *   - @ref async — coroutine and callback plumbing.
 *   - @ref logging — routing diagnostics into the host application's log.
 * - @ref adapter_api — framework integration.
 *   - @ref writing_an_adapter — supporting a new framework.
 *   - @ref adapter_interfaces — the interfaces an adapter implements.
 *   - @ref drogon_adapter — the bundled Drogon adapter.
 *
 * @section main_examples Examples
 *
 * Runnable programs live in the `examples/` directory of the source tree:
 *
 * - `CheckoutSessionCli` — creates a Checkout session from the command line.
 * - `BillingPortalCli` — creates a billing portal session.
 * - `WebhookSignature` — the smallest possible verified webhook endpoint.
 * - `DrogonCheckoutDemo` — the full flow inside a Drogon server.
 *
 * @section main_more Project documentation
 *
 * - @ref versioning — versioning policy and release tag format.
 *
 * Build instructions and test setup are in the project `README.md`.
 *
 * @section main_license License
 *
 * BSD-3-Clause. See `LICENSE`.
 */
